    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the per-city capacity rule for `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is now rejected with **409 Conflict** when its city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold`/`DuplicateHouseholdException` pattern), I added:\n\n- **`EnsureCityBelowCapacity`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 a pipeline step that counts existing owners whose city matches the request's (compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace) and throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the count reaches 50.\n- **`CityAtCapacityException`** (checked, `extends Exception`) \u2014 carries the city and count.\n- **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `409` with an `errors.city` message body, matching the household handler's shape.\n- **`.../escalation/...CityAtCapacityException.yml`** \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n- Updated **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `ensureCityBelowCapacity` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) after `ensureUniqueHousehold` and before `build`, so the capacity check runs against committed data before the new owner is constructed.\n\nThe pre-existing acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a fresh city to exactly 50, then expects the 51st to be a 409) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
